// Package batch, file vaultindex_test.go — T-25 characterization
// (Phase 2): the VaultIndex half.
//
// THE LAW: the Python characterization tests are ported FIRST, then the
// code; the goldens were GENERATED by running the unmodified Python
// reference app (assadigit/GitCurator @ 98f4fc7) via
// testdiff/goldens/dump_linktracker.py — never hand-typed. Regenerate
// with:
//
//	python3 testdiff/goldens/dump_linktracker.py
//
// Ported/landed suites:
//   - test_onespelling.py: TestTheVaultIndexKeys — one note answers
//     both spellings (the note is hand-written with the same
//     frontmatter keys build_website_note produces; the index only
//     reads source:/managed_by:/fetch_status:, and the pipeline's
//     builder is Phase-4 T-40 territory).
//   - test_lawfix.py: TestTrashSkipLists.test_vault_index_skips_trash.
//   - test_intakefix.py: TestMissingRepoNote.
//     test_vault_index_dedupes_through_the_note (via notebuilder's
//     ported BuildMissingRepoNote) — plus the _inbox skip the
//     TestInboxTableRouting leg pins.
//   - The generated corpora: TestLinktrackerPureGolden (the manifest
//     BYTES — the Go writer's json.dump(indent=2) byte-parity pin —
//     and the SafeMocName battery), TestLinktrackerObsidianGolden (the
//     env-steered find_obsidian_vaults battery), and
//     TestLinktrackerBehaviorGolden (the skip sets, quote stripping,
//     the 4000-char boundary, the site_links grammar, the site-map
//     gates, add_url's incremental learn — the reference's own answers
//     over the same crafted vaults).
